    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d319">

                <pb facs="0303" n="283" sameAs="frus:frus1864p3/pg283"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr. Clay</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 58.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-02-01"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >February</hi> 1, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your despatch of the 5th of January last, and to thank you, in the
                    President’s name, for the generous sentiments which you have expressed in regard
                    to his policy and his health.</p>
                <p>The experiment of reconstruction is begun in Louisiana, Arkansas, and Tennessee
                    under what seem to be favorable auspices. The legislature of Maryland has
                    provided for taking the sense of the people of that State upon the question of
                    emancipation.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Cassius M. Clay</hi>, Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
